The commit introduces the vulnerable construct in `xway_gphy_config_init` on lines 291-293: 

c
	/* Use default LED configuration if 'leds' node isn't defined */
	if (!of_get_child_by_name(np, "leds"))
		xway_gphy_init_leds(phydev);


Here, `of_get_child_by_name` is called to check for the existence of the "leds" child node. When the node exists, it returns a pointer with an incremented reference count, but this reference is never released with `of_node_put()`, causing an OF device node reference leak.
